76, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "Node 303 emits only 3 events in the window (out-neighbours 1409, 1465, 1583; step_02/03), localized to ~[46896,47495], ~[52896,53495] and ~[63696,64295] (step_10). Node 1293 receives from only 28, 1438, 1574 (step_04), with inbound events near ~43.3k, ~45.1k, ~47.5-48.1k and ~52.3-52.9k (step_11). None of 303's out-neighbours contacts 1293 directly (step_15 shows 1409-1293 has no events at all). Following the only temporally viable branch forward with the 600-unit delay constraint: 303->1409 (~47.4k) -> 1409->960 -> 960->254 (steps 12,14,16); 254 is not an in-neighbour of 1293, so the chain drifts away from the target and terminates. The later 303 events (~53k, ~64k) start after or far from 1293's inbound activity, so no delay-respecting continuation exists. The graph is large and 303/1293 are weakly connected when time is ignored (step_01, step_05), but that static reachability is not backed by an admissible time-respecting path. Conclusion: no genuine cascade from 303 to 1293."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_b6ce5479\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [303, 1293, 1409, 960, 254],\n  \"window\": [28296, 66695],\n  \"confidence\": 0.76,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Node 303 emits only 3 events in the window (out-neighbours 1409, 1465, 1583; step_02/03), localized to ~[46896,47495], ~[52896,53495] and ~[63696,64295] (step_10). Node 1293 receives from only 28, 1438, 1574 (step_04), with inbound events near ~43.3k, ~45.1k, ~47.5-48.1k and ~52.3-52.9k (step_11). None of 303's out-neighbours contacts 1293 directly (step_15 shows 1409-1293 has no events at all). Following the only temporally viable branch forward with the 600-unit delay constraint: 303->1409 (~47.4k) -> 1409->960 -> 960->254 (steps 12,14,16); 254 is not an in-neighbour of 1293, so the chain drifts away from the target and terminates. The later 303 events (~53k, ~64k) start after or far from 1293's inbound activity, so no delay-respecting continuation exists. The graph is large and 303/1293 are weakly connected when time is ignored (step_01, step_05), but that static reachability is not backed by an admissible time-respecting path. Conclusion: no genuine cascade from 303 to 1293.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 61017, "total_output_tokens": 6619, "total_tokens": 67636, "total_latency_ms": 95502, "llm_calls": 10, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}